  "id": "COMPOUND:156 - PROTEIN:6020",
  "verbalization": "Lipoic acid appears to act as a target of multiple compounds that ultimately influence the activity of PITSLRE serine/threonine-protein kinase CDC2L1. This relationship is mediated through UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B10, which serves as a common intermediate in the pathways involving lipoic acid, acetamide, sennoside D, and 9-isovaleroxy balanophonin. These compounds likely modulate the enzyme's function through distinct mechanisms, yet all converge on the same target. The evidence suggests that lipoic acid may exert its effects via indirect pathways, where it influences the activity of UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B10, which in turn affects the kinase CDC2L1. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential role for lipoic acid in regulating kinase activity through a network of metabolic and enzymatic interactions.",
